💡 One of the biggest reasons Docker is so popular is that it solves the classic "It works on my machine" problem. By packaging an application along with its dependencies, Docker ensures that it runs consistently across different environments.
⚡ Why is Docker lightweight?
Unlike traditional Virtual Machines (VMs), Docker containers do not require a full guest operating system. Instead, they share the host OS kernel, which provides:
• Faster startup times
• Lower memory consumption
• Better resource utilization
• The ability to run more applications on the same machine
This makes Docker an excellent choice for modern application development, testing, deployment, and microservices architectures.
